# ABOUTME: Code owners for the WJD group repository.
# ABOUTME: Combined with "Require review from Code Owners", makes review mandatory.
#
# When a pull request touches a path, GitHub automatically assigns the matching
# owners as reviewers.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: the last rule that matches is the one that applies.
#
# Two principles here. Each area has a maintainer alongside the repo owner, so
# review lands on whoever knows that part. And every rule lists at least two
# owners: the author of a pull request cannot approve their own pull request, so
# a single-owner rule would leave every change proposed by that owner without a
# possible reviewer, blocking the merge.

# Whole repository: every pull request needs a teammate's approval.
